L2591 datasheet from the manufacturer's site.\n\nFrom general knowledge, not from this file, here are the values I'd expect. Please verify them against the official datasheet before relying on them:\n\n1. **COMMAND:** CMD is bit 7 (set to 1), TRANSACTION is bits 6–5, and ADDR/SF is bits 4–0. Normal register read/write uses TRANSACTION = 01, so the command byte is 0xA0 | register address.\n2. **Registers:** ENABLE 0x00, CONFIG 0x01, STATUS 0x13, ID 0x12 (expected 0x50), C0DATAL 0x14, C0DATAH 0x15, C1DATAL 0x16, C1DATAH 0x17. I'm not certain the datasheet calls the config register \"CONTROL.\"\n3. **ENABLE bits:** PON bit 0, AEN bit 1, AIEN bit 4, NPIEN bit 7.\n4. **CONFIG:** AGAIN is bits 5–4: 00 = low (1×), 01 = medium (25×), 10 = high (428×), 11 = maximum (9876×). ATIME is bits 2–0, with integration time = (ATIME + 1) × 100 ms, giving 100 ms through 600 ms.\n5. **Max count:** 36863 at 100 ms; 65535 at 200–600 ms.\n6. **STATUS:** AVALID is bit 0.\n7. **Channels:** C0 is full spectrum (visible + IR), and C1 is IR only. I believe reading the low byte latches the high byte, but I'm less certain of that detail.\n8. **I2C address:** 0x29 (7-bit).\n</fetched-web-content>\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 705.5KB) was saved to a local file for the caller. You cannot open files here, and the harness gives the caller the path itself — say that the file was saved, but do not put any file path in your report.]"}]},"uuid":"72535c5e-3858-4ba1-b089-60eb565de6b7","timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:42:24.607Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5542df74-991c-4ec9-9a79-b938fc18aea2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/nicholasmarechal/Desktop/CS 370/Term Project","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"nickmarechal/Term-Project---Stargazing-Sensor-","visibility":"public"}]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/Users/nicholasmarechal/Desktop/CS 370/Term P